<mn>224.5</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>. Unanticipated production predicts\nshorter strikes, at about the evidence a <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"t\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D461 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> statistic of three provides; the\nPoisson analysis overstates that by orders of magnitude.</p>","file":"ch38-quasi-likelihood/04-overdispersion.html"}